        "description": "An oil and/or gas lease is an agreement between a mineral owner (lessor) and a company (lessee) in which the owner grants the company the right to explore, drill and produce oil, gas, and other minerals below the surface of the earth. Oil and gas leases are created so that property owner can maintain their mineral rights while leasing their land to an extraction company.<div><br /></div><div>The <a href='https://kgs.ku.edu' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Kansas Geological Survey</a> maintains and publishes this GIS data. The Kansas Department of Revenue is the data originator, and they send updates to the KGS monthly.</div>",
